<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia March palm oil output up 33 pct - MOPGC.</title>
<headline>Malaysia March palm oil output up 33 pct - MOPGC.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Malaysian Oil Palm Growers' Council (MOPGC) has estimated Malaysia's crude palm oil output in March at 670,000 tonnes, up 33 percent from February, traders who obtained the data said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Private crop forecaster Ivan Wong had estimated March production at 665,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The Palm Oil Registration and Licensing Authority is due to release official March crop data at 0430 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-206-2323)</p>
</text>
